overlap.

184
00:24:50,780 --> 00:25:00,980
When we are looking at backwards looking
accounting metrics, this is, of course,
defined as quantitative work.

185
00:25:02,060 --> 00:25:19,380
However, because it's backwards looking,
it is also working on evidence to support
forward looking valuation and to
potentially discover what is behind
revenue growth and earnings growth for
positive and negative outliers.

186
00:25:19,380 --> 00:25:34,020
But when we are doing qualitative
processes, qualitative work on a stock,
naturally, by doing that, we are also
engaging in learning about the stock's
information.

187
00:25:34,720 --> 00:25:37,320
So this is also evidence work.

188
00:25:37,880 --> 00:25:42,440
And this can be both backwards and
forwards looking.

189
00:25:43,440 --> 00:25:55,720
And when we are doing qualitative work on
a stock and on a sector, we are also
looking forwards and we are identifying
key performance indicators.

190
00:25:55,720 --> 00:26:09,280
So with KPIs, we are identifying the
drivers of the drivers of the business
behind revenue and earnings.

191
00:26:09,280 --> 00:26:20,040
And with identifying catalysts, we are
identifying what is going to drive the
stock and what is going to drive
valuation.

192
00:26:20,040 --> 00:26:30,120
But this next part of the microeconomic
processes that we utilize is coming up in
the next part of the PTM video series.

193
00:26:30,120 --> 00:26:34,340
We're going to be obviously looking at
qualitative processes.

194
00:26:34,900 --> 00:26:45,120
Now, you'll recall that we looked at a
theoretical long short portfolio and that
was built all based on earnings growth
profiles.

195
00:26:45,120 --> 00:27:03,200
So we had our theoretical 10 stock,
$100,000 portfolio with a net long bias
that's non beta adjusted, but it was all
built on the assumption of only looking at
earnings growth profiles.

196
00:27:03,200 --> 00:27:07,680
So we obviously jumped the gun here.

197
00:27:07,680 --> 00:27:27,280
There is still a lot more work to do if we
build a portfolio only based on earnings
growth profiles, which, by the way, we
will never do this assumes that we haven't
done any qualitative processes at all.

198
00:27:27,280 --> 00:27:35,440
And that we don't want our stocks to move
in the next 20 to 60 days.

199
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:39,440
So our stocks don't actually have
catalysts.

200
00:27:39,440 --> 00:27:56,960
As traders and portfolio managers, we want
to know what is behind the numbers, what
is behind the revenue growth, what is
behind the earnings growth, what is
driving that, and also what is driving
valuation.

201
00:27:56,960 --> 00:28:07,680
And what we also want to know is we want
to know if there are catalysts that are
going to move the stock within our time
horizon.

202
00:28:09,040 --> 00:28:16,160
Remember, we must always know the
difference between a trade idea and an
investment idea.

203
00:28:16,160 --> 00:28:26,400
We absolutely must never forget that a
trade idea is not an investment idea nor a
day trade.

204
00:28:26,400 --> 00:28:31,280
We are operating in the 20 to 60 day time
horizon.

205
00:28:31,280 --> 00:28:34,320
We are long short portfolio managers.

206
00:28:34,320 --> 00:28:39,040
We want to be right by 60 days out.

207
00:28:39,040 --> 00:28:47,840
We do not come up with investment ideas
and we do not turn our trade ideas into
investments.

208
00:28:47,840 --> 00:28:54,480
We must know what is driving the numbers,
what is behind the numbers.

209
00:28:54,480 --> 00:29:08,800
We must know, we must understand before we
even go into a trade, what is going to
move the needle within our time horizon on
the numbers.

210
00:29:09,360 --> 00:29:18,320
What behind the numbers is going to move
the needle and what is the catalyst or
catalysts that are going to achieve that.

211
00:29:19,520 --> 00:29:26,480
And we must never forget also that the
quality of our ideas is paramount.

212
00:29:26,480 --> 00:29:38,880
Never forget the importance that the
quality of our trade ideas plays in the
overall process of building and managing a
long-short portfolio.

213
00:29:40,480 --> 00:29:52,800
So this is why we go through all of our
processes, not just, for example, going
through the identification stage of the
quantitative process,

214
00:29:53,760 --> 00:30:01,920
finding something that is high PE and high
earnings growth, and then turning it into
a position.

215
00:30:01,920 --> 00:30:09,040
We obviously have to go through a lot more
processes and do a lot more work than just
that stage.

216
00:30:09,040 --> 00:30:11,600
That is just an identification process.

217
00:30:12,800 --> 00:30:15,280
It's a discovery process.

218
00:30:15,280 --> 00:30:20,160
And then we move on to the next part of
our quantitative process.

219
00:30:20,800 --> 00:30:24,960
The next part of our quant phase, which is
evidence.

220
00:30:24,960 --> 00:30:34,160
We look to backwards looking quantitative
metrics for evidence to support the
forward looking quant.

221
00:30:35,440 --> 00:30:41,840
And in the process, we are obviously, even
at that stage, learning about the stock
information.

222
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:50,160
And even then, we don't stop and turn
something into a position, turn a trade
idea into a position.

223
00:30:51,120 --> 00:30:53,920
At that stage, it's not even a trade idea
yet.

224
00:30:54,560 --> 00:30:58,000
We then move on to the qualitative
processes.

225
00:30:58,880 --> 00:31:02,640
We identify the drivers behind the
numbers.

226
00:31:03,920 --> 00:31:14,880
And this helps us understand and pinpoint
what is going to drive the valuation of
the stock going forwards.

227
00:31:14,880 --> 00:31:17,600
And what is going to drive price.

228
00:31:18,160 --> 00:31:26,560
And not only that, it's going to help us
understand and even pinpoint what is going
to move the needle

229
00:31:27,200 --> 00:31:28,960
within our time horizon.

230
00:31:30,640 --> 00:31:37,760
A trade idea is not a trade idea if you
have only done the quantitative work.

231
00:31:38,400 --> 00:31:47,040
The definition of a trade idea, a complete
trade idea, is when you have done both the
quantitative

232
00:31:47,040 --> 00:31:49,600
and the qualitative assessment.

233
00:31:51,440 --> 00:31:58,160
So, with that being said, let's move on to
the next part of the PTM video series.

234
00:31:58,720 --> 00:32:04,160
Let's move on to the qualitative
processes.
